<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zog I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1895">1895</a>–<a href="/years/1961">1961</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ahmet Zogu, King Zog, Zog I of Albania</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zog I, born Ahmet Zogu, was an Albanian chieftain from Mat who dominated his country's politics between the wars. He overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fan-noli">Fan Noli</a>'s government in December 1924, became president of the Albanian Republic in 1925 and proclaimed himself King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albanians">Albanians</a> in 1928. He drew Albania closely towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fascist-italy">Fascist Italy</a>, which invaded in April 1939 and drove him into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zog-i.jpg" alt="Zog I" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was J.J. at English Wikipedia.; Tonysmith at zh.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Zog_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Mussolini's forces landed at Durrës and other ports, and within days <b>King Zog</b> had fled.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-7">7 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>On 1 September 1928 a constituent assembly turned the Albanian Republic into a kingdom, and President <b>Ahmet Zogu</b> became Zog I, King of the Albanians, a title chosen to suggest claims beyond the state's borders.</blockquote><a href="/state/albanian-kingdom">Albanian Kingdom</a></li><li><blockquote>Italy invaded Albania on 7 April 1939, forcing <b>King Zog</b> of the Albanian Kingdom into exile.</blockquote><a href="/state/albanian-kingdom-1939-1943">Albanian Kingdom (1939-1943)</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Ahmet Zogu</b>, a chieftain from Mat, was driven out by Fan Noli's June Revolution of 1924 but returned in December with support from the Kingdom of Yugoslavia and White Russian mercenaries.</blockquote><a href="/state/albanian-republic">Albanian Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>The 1920s saw instability, with Fan Noli's June Revolution of 1924 overthrown by <b>Ahmet Zogu</b> in December.</blockquote><a href="/state/principality-of-albania">Principality of Albania</a></li><li><blockquote>Albanian government forces, with commanders including <b>Ahmet Zogu</b>, crushed the revolt in November 1921, while the Conference of Ambassadors confirmed Albania's 1913 borders, ending Yugoslav claims.</blockquote><a href="/state/republic-of-mirdita">Republic of Mirdita</a></li></ul></section>
